  "title": "Cross-modal Oddball Task.",
  "description": "EEG dataset from 146 participants (98 with Parkinson's disease and 48 controls) performing a cross-modal oddball task collected between 2017 and 2021. Each trial presented simultaneous visual and auditory pre-cues, either standard or oddball, followed by a directional arrow GO cue requiring a response. The dataset supports investigation of midfrontal neural activity and cognitive dysfunction in Parkinson's disease.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a 64-channel BrainVision cap during an oddball task with a primary GO cue (white arrow) requiring a directional response. Visual and auditory pre-cues occurred simultaneously 500 ms before the arrow cue. Trials had standard pre-cues, an oddball visual pre-cue, or an oddball auditory pre-cue.",
